  </div>
</section>
<section data-sect="" data-pad="" style="max-width:1440px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 72px 100px;"><div data-cols="" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.15fr;gap:70px;align-items:start">
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px"><div style="font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:500;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5CF6">The problem</div><h2 data-h2="" data-rv="" style="margin:0;font-family:Sora,sans-serif;font-size:38px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.1">Presentable is not the same as persuasive.</h2></div>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#A1A1AA">Most business sites are assembled from a template and filled with whatever content already existed. They look acceptable and perform poorly: visitors cannot find what they came for, the mobile experience arrives second, and no page offers an obvious next step.</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#A1A1AA">Custom work is not decoration. It is arranging information so a visitor understands the offer, believes it, and arrives at the action that matters to the business.</p></div>
</div></section>
<section data-sect="" data-pad="" style="max-width:1440px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 72px 100px;"><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px;padding:48px;border-radius:28px;background:#0B0B0E;border:1px solid rgba(248,250,252,.08)">
